# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Next copies public/ into out/ verbatim, so
# this file ends up where Pages looks for it.
#
# The comparison stopped being a page of its own when it became a view of the
# playground. Links to it are older than the merge, so the route still exists
# in the export and forwards on its own — this is the same forward one hop
# earlier, as a real 301, for the search engines and for the reader who should
# not have to boot a page to leave it.
#
# Paths only: these rules cannot match a hostname, which is why serving the
# playground at the root of playground.heddle.run is a Function instead.
/compare   /playground?view=compare   301
/compare/  /playground?view=compare   301
